    "body": "Opportunities for batch allocation are something that I stumble upon quite regularly and usually there's more than one allocation going on in the loop. Most recently in real code [here](https://github.com/rip-create-your-account/finnishtable/blob/922be3edd01262805c3c716a0bd1993890a7ca57/map.go#L186-L190).\r\n\r\nI really don't like doing `batch := make([]T, n); obj1 := &batch[0]; obj2 := &batch[1]; ...` for the reasons already mentioned in the OP, but it improves performance on all metrics too much to not do it. Please guide us away from the temptation of one-at-a-time processing.",
